  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The museum has an object, a written local story, and a question inviting visitors’ reflections.\", \"decision\": \"How should visitors encounter a local story?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVisitors consider the reflection question before exploring the object and story. Their own initial response guides what they notice.\nVisitors read the story before seeing the object and answering the reflection question. The narrative provides context for the object.\nVisitors see the object before reading the story and answering the reflection question. The physical example gives the story an initial point of reference."
    }
